## New ambiguity: AMB-031
- **(a) The ulp₃₂ definition awaits owner confirmation.** It is implemented exactly as D12 proposes. Open question: whether "above the binary32 range" means |x| > FLT_MAX (my choice) or |x| ≥ 2¹²⁸.
- **(b) Overall verdict with non-comparable positions.** Following your brief, they are excluded and listed but don't by themselves block a pass. A consumer reading only `verdict` could miss them; under OQ6 each still has to be traced.
- **(c)–(i) Smaller choices:**
  - the band format (an evaluated position in no band is refused);
  - row index = absolute position, and D12's "unsupported or resource-limited" outcome is not modelled;
  - which ref₃₂-to-ref₆₄ fields must match (thread counts are not compared);
  - a token-id hash is required on the candidate record;
  - how positions are validated;
  - c and k are taken at their exact values (a float `0.1` is not 1/10);
  - `worst_ratio` is a rounded diagnostic only, so a ratio shown as 1.0 can sit beside an exactly decided `fail`.
